{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The differential equation is separable.\n\nWhat does it look like after we separate the variables?","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\dfrac{dy}{y+1}=dt$\n\nLet's integrate both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\displaystyle\\int\\dfrac{dy}{y+1}=\\int dt$\n\nWhat do we get?","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\ln|y+1|=t + C$\n\nWhat value of $C$ satisfies the initial condition $y(0)=3$?","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's substitute $t=0$ and $y=3$ into the equation and solve for $C$.\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\ln|3+1|\u0026=0 + C\\\\\n\\\\\nC\u0026=\\ln 4\n\\end{align}$\n\nNow use this value of $C$ to find $t$ when $y=1$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\\ln|1+1|\u0026=t + \\ln 4\\\\\n\\\\\nt\u0026=\\ln 2-\\ln 4\\\\\n\\\\\nt\u0026=\\ln 2-2\\ln 2\\\\\n\\\\\nt\u0026=-\\ln 2\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$\\dfrac{dy}{dt}=y+1$ and $y(0)=3$.\n\n**What is $t$ when $y=1$?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$t=0$","correct":false},{"content":"$t=1$","correct":false},{"content":"$t=-\\ln 2$","correct":true},{"content":"$t=\\ln 2$","correct":false},{"content":"$t=\\ln 4$","correct":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":true,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
